\begin{align*}
\text{Percentage change} &= \frac{\Delta F}{F_{1900}} \times 100 \\
&= \frac{1}{4.5} \times 100 \\
&\approx \boxed{22.22\%}
\end{align*}

Therefore, the estimated total number of children born to a woman in her lifetime in 1900 is approximately 4.5, and in 1960, it is approximately 3.5. The percentage change in the total number of children born between these two time periods is approximately 22.22%.

